<!--Post: 7829--><!--Time: 1108699407-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7829"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brown_tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brown_tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 8:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->1. Why does a killer want to keep something from a victim? ie..D.L., necklace... <BR>For his own pleasure, or a way to prove something later maybe? <BR> <BR>2. Do you think BTK takes a specific thing each time he commits murder, or something unique each time to each person? Of course, we already know he has or had several of the victim&#39;s D.L.&#39;s. <BR> <BR>3. What do you think BTK actually has in his possession from each victim/crime scene?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
