<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8305"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Puzzler<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Puzzler<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 8:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think the pictures BTK took of the victim&#40;s&#41; are the real treasures he possesses.  That&#39;s why he only sent copies of the pictures of Wegerle.  Maybe giving up the jewelry, DL&#39;s, etc. are just to prove he had them.  Including copies of victim pictures would be a sure way of &#39;claiming credit&#39; for the crime.  IMO, if he took pictures of Mrs. Wegerle, he would have taken picture of all the victims.  I know that&#39;s assuming something not in evidence, but I think that is the proof of undeniability in BTK claiming victims.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
